From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Publish and archive

A post has a status: from draft to published, from published to
archived. One way.

- The rule is a Go method beside the model: func (p Post) Next(to
  string) error. It is not a tag; code says a rule best
- Two routes: POST /posts/{id}/publish and /archive. Both views call
  one move, with their tx:

      func Publish(ctx context.Context, tx maago.Tx, in PostIn) (maago.Result[PostPage], error)

  move reads with GetPost, asks Next, and writes with UpdatePost
- Outside the rule, the view returns maago.Status(http.StatusConflict,
  err): a 409. An HTML route shows the status text alone, not err (an
  API route puts it in the problem's detail). The error rolls the
  transaction back
- UpdatePost has a 409 of its own. UpdatedAt (auto=update) is the
  post's version: UpdatePost writes only while the row still has the
  version it was read with, and otherwise returns maago.ErrConflict,
  which is a 409 too. Two who read the same post and both write: the
  second does not undo the first unseen. The test writes from a stale
  copy
- The post page draws only the button for where it may go now: {{if eq
  .Post.Status "draft"}}

Hiding a button does not stop a request sent by hand; Next does. The
test sends the requests the rule refuses, with no button.

diff --git a/board/models.go b/board/models.go
index d91f180..6ba06ee 100644
--- a/board/models.go
+++ b/board/models.go
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 package board
 
 import (
+	"fmt"
 	"time"
 
 	"github.com/maago-web/maago"
@@ -42,3 +43,15 @@ type Comment struct {
 	Text      string
 	CreatedAt time.Time `maago:"auto=create"`
 }
+
+// next is where a post of each status may go: draft, then published, then
+// archived, one way.
+var next = map[string]string{"draft": "published", "published": "archived"}
+
+// Next reports whether p may become status to.
+func (p Post) Next(to string) error {
+	if next[p.Status] != to {
+		return fmt.Errorf("a %s post cannot become %s", p.Status, to)
+	}
+	return nil
+}
